# Copy to .env and fill in ONE key. Never commit .env.
#
# The assistant's only job is turning messy recipe text into structured JSON.
# That is a small job, and a free model does it well — so pick whichever of
# these you can get a key for. Set exactly one; Mise detects which and uses it.
#
# ── free, no credit card ───────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Google Gemini — https://aistudio.google.com/apikey
#   Generous daily allowance. The safe default.
# GEMINI_API_KEY=

# Groq — https://console.groq.com/keys
#   Runs open models very fast. Lower daily cap than Gemini.
# GROQ_API_KEY=

# Cerebras — https://cloud.cerebras.ai
#   Big token-per-day allowance, fewer requests per minute. Good for long pages.
# CEREBRAS_API_KEY=

# OpenRouter — https://openrouter.ai/keys
#   One key, many models. Its free models have a low daily cap.
# OPENROUTER_API_KEY=

# ── paid ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=sk-ant-...
# OPENAI_API_KEY=sk-...

# Override the model ONLY if you know you want a specific one. Each provider
# already has a sensible default, so leaving this commented out is correct.
#
# A model name belongs to exactly one vendor. Setting a Claude model name while
# using a Gemini key gives you a confusing 404 — a valid key, the right
# endpoint, and a name Google has never heard of. Mise now detects that case,
# ignores the mismatched name, and says so on the health endpoint — but the
# cleanest answer is to leave this line alone.
# MISE_MODEL=
